  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SeABank Housing</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Stakeholder effects: Increased access to housing finance. IFC anticipates that the Project will help address the lack of mortgage finance in Vietnam, particularly for the middle- and lower-income segments. 
Market Creation Competitiveness: IFC anticipates the investment will demonstrate the commercial viability of housing finance, including for the middle- and lower-income earners, and will result in greater market competitiveness through demonstration and replication.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed investment is a senior loan of up to US$100 million for a tenor of up to 5 years to Southeast Asia Commercial Joint-Stock Bank (SeABank or the Bank), with the proceeds exclusively used for supporting the growth of the Banks housing portfolio, including affordable housing (the Project).</narrative>
  </description>
